 **Your browser script** (written by you, Python-free: node with the project's `playwright-core`, in your scratch, not in the repo): a FRESH browser context per (server, level, width); the level chosen by clicking the real start-page button on UAT; viewports **1440 x 900, 820 x 1180, 390 x 844 and 360 x 740** for the logon pages and the header sweep; Chromium headless. Record in a JSON file under `Briefs/2026-10-26_B730_evidence/` per cell: URL, status, final URL, header row count (nav top below brand bottom), header height, the logo's `getBoundingClientRect`, `naturalWidth`/`naturalHeight`, `complete`, `alt`, the old-heading check below, console errors, failed requests, and the count of non-loopback requests aborted.
 **2a. Logon pages: TOP CENTRE.** Three renders, SIGNED OUT, each at the four widths: the UAT start page (9916 `/`), the mock sign-in (9915 `/`), the Entra sign-in page (9917 `/`; also `/workspace` signed out, which redirects to `/?next=%2Fworkspace`). FAIL per cell: no `img` with alt `HP Cyber Security Services Reseller Playbook` (the gate pins the alt string from the head's `HpLogo.tsx`, read with a program); more than one such image; the image's horizontal centre not within 2 px of the viewport's centre; its top not within the first 200 px of the page; it is not the first element of `main`'s content (its top is not above the page `h1`'s top); `complete` false or `naturalWidth` not 950; rendered ratio off: `|w - h*950/221| > 1` or `|h - w*221/950| > 1` px; `documentElement.scrollWidth > viewport width`. Record what sits under the logo (the page `h1`, its lead): see Check 4.
