nd link** (read `textContent` and `innerText`; control: the same program on the head file's removed line, loaded as a string, finds it); the page has no `header` at all where one is expected; `complete` false or `naturalWidth` not 950; ratio off (as 2a); `scrollWidth` greater than the viewport; a failed request or a console error (list each). **A page that still shows the old heading in its header is a finding (Blocker); the old text in page or document content is a Note.** For every page also record the count of occurrences of the old heading text in the whole `body` text and where (this is the D-4 list as RENDERED; compare it to the builder's source list: `HomeScreen.tsx:13,19`, `PartnerDashboard.tsx:159`, `PlaybookHome.tsx:24`, `PlaybookShell.tsx:26`, `DesignSystemScreen.tsx:43`, `phase-flow.ts:66`, `PackView.tsx:61`, `DocumentGeneration.tsx:167`, `ReportScreen.tsx:67`, the logon `h1`s, the tab). Re-run the head census by `git grep -n -F 'HP Security Services Playbook' a660c5cd -- 'web/src/*.ts' 'web/src/*.tsx'` minus test files, with the zero control (`zzz-no-such-7f3a` prints 0); the builder says 15 lines in 12 files at the head (17 in 14 at the base); a render path with the text in a header that the list lacks is a Blocker.
