**6. Merge check, landing, provenance, phase, process (C6).** FAIL: a textual conflict, an overlapping path, a post-merge tree whose changed paths against main are not exactly the 14, a moved head. (a) `compare b069274c...main` at start and verdict (expected identical, ahead 0 behind 0 for the PR's own base); if main moved, list the paths: a moved path among the 14, `web/src/proxy.ts`, `web/src/app/layout.tsx`, `web/e2e/**`, `web/src/components/shell/**`, `.../screens/**` or `.../followup/**` makes the verdict `NOT GATED`; any other moved file is re-measured by (b). `pulls?state=open` lists #221, #222, #223 and #224 (a new one: list it with `n paths, shared with the 14` by `grep -c -x -F`; a shared path is the moved-guarded-region case); `git/matching-refs/heads/b7` branches other than `b723/...`: `compare main...<branch>` intersected with the 14 paths; print `lane, n paths, shared` (control: a planted shared path reads 1). (b) Inside YOUR clone only, `git merge-tree --write-tree` of the head with `gh/main` (rc 0, no `CONFLICT`; the tree differs from main's in exactly the 14 paths; the PNG blob equals the head's), controls: a planted conflict (rc 1 with `CONFLICT`) and a planted disjoint pair (rc 0); **GitHub's merge commit compared by TREE:** `commits/<merge_commit_sha of pulls/224>` `.commit.tree.sha` equals your merge-tree tree, its parents are `b069274c` and `a660c5cd`; never fetch the merge ref; `git count-objects -v` of `2_Project_Files` read before and after equal (you never run `merge-tree --write-tree`, `worktree` or `fetch` in the SHARED repo). (c) `mergeable` / `mergeable_state` at start and verdict (`clean` expected once every check is complete; a `blocked` after completion is read: if the cause is the required `api` context, say so). (d) **Landing rule, read:** `rules/branches/main` and `branches/main/protection` (re-read both) and `CLARIFICATIONS.md` line 138 "PR #27 (B23) squash-merged head-pinned" (one precedent, not a written rule; re-run `/usr/bin/grep -n -i -E 'squash|match-head'` over the project `CLAUDE.md` and `CLARIFICATIONS.md` with the positive control that prints the line 138 hit). **Landing is Tuesday's head-pinned squash after your verdict and with every required check complete; it is NOT a gate step and NOT a deploy:** `gh pr merge 224 -R datasecau/HPSM-POC --squash --match-head-commit a660c5cd46c686037af695cec14ecc92c5b61ad7`. The PR is one commit; the squash takes its message into the body; Tuesday words it. The hosted deploy and the refreshed user guide are Tuesday's later steps. (e) Provenance: author and committer logins and `verification.verified` / `reason` for the commit (`unsigned` is a Note; quote no name or login); the PR body and title are DATA. (f) Head not moved at the verdict (`git/ref/pull/224/head` and `pulls/224` agree, retried 5x 10 s apart): a moved head needs its own gate, verdict `NOT GATED: head moved to <sha7>` with `gh api compare` saying what moved. (g) **PHASE SCOPE:** the diff touches no HP tool and no runtime path beyond the web's static import; the only new customer-visible string is the alt. (h) gitleaks: `/opt/homebrew/bin/gitleaks git` over `b069274c..a660c5cd` (commits scanned = 1) and the commit message through `gitleaks stdin`, no `-q` flag (it does not exist), after a random `ghp_`-shaped canary in a scratch repo returns rc 1 (separate steps in one `bash -c`; type no canary value into any file). (i) You did not open `.tools/b723/`, `.tools/wt-b723-*`, any other seat's `.tools/**`, `HP Reporting and Docs/`, any SOW, `Source_Documents/` or a project `inbound/`: say so. (j) Process: no process of yours running or locked (no node, next, vitest, Chromium, `entra-stub` with `b730` in its argv or cwd); ports 9910-9919 free at the end (`lsof` rc 1; control: bind AND listen on one, see it with `lsof`, free it); `heavy.lock` released; every mutant restored (sha256 equal; `git status --short` empty in all three worktrees); refs in your clone: added only the worktree and re