## SEVERITY / VERDICT (the grading rule is decided HERE; apply it, do not re-argue it)
*Blocker:* a path beyond the 14, or an `api/`, `infra/`, `.github/`, `proxy.ts`, `next.config.ts`, `package.json`, lockfile, `styles/**` or `layout.tsx` byte; the PNG not byte-equal (blob or served bytes) to the product owner's file; a non-ASCII byte, a person's name, a decision-card id, a `B###` token or a `HPSMPOC-` key in an added line or the message; a skip, sleep, retry loop or environment gate added to a test; **the instruction not met in a real browser: a logon page (any of the three renders) without the logo, or with it off-centre by more than 2 px, or not at the top, or broken (`naturalWidth` 0, or a redirect or non-200 or non-`image/png` answer for the asset signed out); an app page or the client page whose header lacks the logo at the top left, or still shows the old heading text in its header; a distorted logo (ratio off by more than 1 px); a missing or different alt; any overflow sideways at any width of the sweep; a new customer-visible word other than the alt;** lint, typecheck or build red at the head; the unit suite red at the head (and the red file not reproduced on the base); a red `web` check-run or e2e shard not shown to be a base-side flake; a red `api` job with any failing test other than the two `PkcsInPackageTests` rows; the head moved; a CodeQL alert open on the head (either threshold) or a missing analysis at the verdict; a textual conflict in Check 6; a secret.
*Major, class SAME (the class is "web header and logon markup swap plus one image asset, web only"):* **(M1) a new test row that cannot fail:** a mutant among m1-m4 that leaves every row green which that row exists to turn red, not shown equivalent by a run; **(M2) an existing pin weakened, not replaced:** a changed assertion (the seven listed in the builder's DESIGN) that now asserts less than before without asserting the logo and the text's absence; **(M3) the trap unproven:** the logo is reachable signed out on the mock server but NOT on the UAT or Entra server (this is the Blocker in 2b; M3 is only the case where 2b could not be run and the unit rows alone were relied on: then the verdict is at most GO WITH FINDINGS with "signed-out load on a gated server NOT MEASURED"); **(M4)** a page in the enumerated set that has an app header the builder's census missed and that still carries the old heading (a Blocker if it is in a header; Major if the text is in a component the builder's list calls content but the page presents as its header).
*Major, class DIFFERENT:* a builder claim contradicted by measurement with a verdict consequence (197 files / 2979 passed / 0 failed; 26 red at base; the logo loaded signed out on three servers; centred within 2 px; ratio; the header sweep counts).
*Minor / Note (never a Major):* the phone header wrap (8 cells two rows, accepted in the builder's D-8); the logo's inner words tiny at 28 px; the mock picker taller than 900 px at 1440; the logon `h1` kept under the logo (N-A); the D-4 pages that keep the product name as content; PNG metadata; the unsigned commit; the PR body's trailer naming a different model than the commit's; one-row cell counts different from the builder's by cells that are Notes; a base-side flake you reproduce on the base; node/npm minor version differences from the runner; `api` required contexts red from the Pkcs cause alone (Note, but landing is then blocked by rule: say so in FOR TUESDAY).
*Where the line between Note and Major is unclear:* a thing that makes a new row unable to fail, or makes the logo absent or broken for a visitor, is at least Major SAME (the second is a Blocker); a thing that changes only how it looks and stays true to the instruction is a Note. Say which rule you applied for every finding.
**VERDICT RULES.** GO needs Checks 1 to 6 clean and measured, both CodeQL thresholds met on a COMPLETE scan (4 of 4 analyses at `a660c5c`, 0 open alerts), every web check-run `completed` `success`, the instruction met on every enumerated page with screenshots opened, 0 findings above Note. **While any check-run of the head is pending the verdict is at most GO WITH FINDINGS and carries `(conditional: CI pending: <names>)`, never a bare GO.** GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note only. NO GO on any Blocker or Major; this is round 1 of 2, so a NO GO here does NOT reach the round cap: STATUS gives each Major's mutant or evidence, the red set by name (or "none: green") and a fix-shape in prose. NOT GATED = the head moved, the PR is not open, or a moved guarded region. A security-shaped finding is a STOP for tier 1.
